', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'al anwaar al lateefah volume 1 the oneness tawheed trust and the science of realities', 'trust and the science of realities before a single doctrine of the oneness is taught the recorder of these lessons stops to say what they are and how they reached us an inherited wisdom drawn not from speculation but from the sciences of the prophets and the friends of allah recorded by explicit permission and deposited in the treasury of the sacred mission he binds the listener with a covenant of safekeeping and names a punishment of cold iron for those who break it then lays out the books symmetrical fivefold architecture and its method to state pure reality directly with no interpretation and no symbol from there the doctrine opens declaring that the oneness of allah is reached by two things only loving allegiance and lawful action and that this is the road by which the exiled soul returns to the homeland of spirits from which it first came', '');
', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'al anwaar al lateefah volume 1 the oneness tawheed the unknowable originator', 'the unknowable originator the opening lesson laid the road home this one turns to face what waits at its end and finds the one toward whom the whole return is directed beyond every reach we have no indication falls upon the originator no thought can bridge the gap to him and the names and attributes we use slide off him entirely since a created name can only characterize its like and never its own maker those names land instead upon the first intellect the first thing he brought forth and the incapacity to know him is shown to be universal shared by the highest intelligence and the lowest body alike the episode closes on the strangest teaching of all that our very word allah is not a description but the cry of a bewildered creation circling a center it cannot comprehend lit up through the famous exchange in which the commander of the faithful says he saw god not with the eye but with insight', '');
', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'al anwaar al lateefah volume 1 the oneness tawheed naming the unnameable', 'naming the unnameable the previous lesson closed on a paradox the first intellect cannot know the originator yet it is the first intellect that first speaks of him this episode follows that speaking to its strange conclusion it opens with the primal act in which the first intellect negated divinity from itself and affirmed it for allah alone the act the quran records as allah testifies that there is no god but he it shows why we name him only out of compelled inadequacy having been given knowledge of life but never knowledge of his essence why the existence he grants is never reclaimed so that his refusal to do injustice is the perfection of his power and why naming the unnameable is a sin that arrives already joined to the asking of forgiveness excused like the woman judged before umar because it is compelled it closes with the ten ascending ranks of the spiritual ladder whose summit is the bare he and the hidden meanings folded into the pairings of prayer', '');
', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'al anwaar al lateefah volume 1 the oneness tawheed what tawhid really is', 'what tawhid really is the volumes boldest move the teaching overturns the most common answer to the most basic question asked what it means to affirm the oneness of allah almost everyone says it means to consider him one and the hudud reply that this taken as a definition is shirk because it subjects the one to number tawhid is something else entirely the gnosis of the ranks the recognition that each rank of the spiritual hierarchy is unique in its place and the knowledge of where each stands and how high it rises because the beings are innumerable this is the highest and most inexhaustible of all knowledge and a souls own station is set by how much of it he attains through his effort meeting the grace from above the episode closes on the three branches of the full saying tawhid the gnosis of the ranks tanzih the denial that any rank can originate and tajrid the stripping of every name and attribute from allah', '');
', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'al anwaar al lateefah volume 1 the oneness tawheed the two gnoses and the mukathir', 'the two gnoses and the mukathir how can a saints most devoted disciple and his sworn enemy know him equally well because the gnosis of the ranks comes in two kinds the outer gnosis knows a ranks person and station and in it the friend and the foe stand on exactly the same footing for both see the same outward man the inner gnosis reaches the beginning the level and the return of a ranks essence and is reserved for the disciplined and the verifying among the people of truth without it the teaching warns a man may have no tawhid at all the episode then maps the approach to the hierarchy two thresholds that are not yet ranks the mustajib who binds himself by the tongue and the mumin who joins tongue heart and limb each with ten levels and the first true rank the mukathir entered by breaking ones own self against the command of allah and the prophet which is why knowledge is indispensable to him', '');
', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'al anwaar al lateefah volume 1 the oneness tawheed the mukathir house of allah', 'the mukathir house of allah what if the holiest man you ever met looked to the eye exactly like everyone else and the whole difference lay in something no inspection could detect the mukathir and the ordinary man are made of the same flesh and blood gathered within the same bodily bounds and yet they are not the same the mukathirs temperament has been refined and his essence purified through an ascent that reaches even into his outward composition though no eye can see it standing at the summit of the human which is the threshold of the spiritual world and holding the command of allah and the prophet before him in every thought word and deed he becomes a house from the houses of allah a place on which revelation descends the qurans houses and the men whom no commerce diverts are these very ranks their establishing of prayer is in its depth the establishing of the divine summons and beneath every pillar of the religion there lies just such an inner meaning the whole law one continuous training of the soul in knowledge and allegiance', '');
', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'al anwaar al lateefah volume 1 the oneness tawheed ascent decline and a god', 'ascent decline and a god two men stand on the same platform made of the same flesh born into the same world and one is rising toward allah while the other is sinking below the level of cattle what separates them is nothing in their composition but only the establishing of prayer in its inner sense the same logic is written into the animal kingdom where lawful and forbidden creatures of one created stuff part ways by their nearness or aversion to man and the obedient and disobedient among men are separated by a distance greater still the mukathirs sensory soul meanwhile has been dyed luminous by the divine sciences flowing into it and where such purity is genuinely present a true rank is genuinely present though it rests hidden with allah at the heart of the episode stands the bewildered disciple for whom his overwhelming teacher has become a god not a creator but the center of the circle around which his astonishment turns', '');
', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'al anwaar al lateefah volume 1 the oneness tawheed the ladder of tawhid', 'the ladder of tawhid if the guide leading you to allah is himself bewildered before someone greater is he still your god or is that bewilderment the thing that points past him the disciple who was left circling his teacher looks upward and sees that the teacher is himself bewildered before the rank above him and that one before the next rank upon rank to the first intellect bewildered before the originator recognizing that bewilderment as the universal condition and as the first step of all knowledge which is the confession that one does not know he negates divinity from every rank and affirms it for allah alone completing tanzih above both the limited and the unlimited ranks and tajrid of every name before returning to his own station and obedience the linked circles of the divine summons and the very letters of the word for god carry this same structure the created gods are told apart from the one true god by their need of a nourisher above them and the tranquil soul is sent home to its lord its serenity the fruit of its gnosis the whole matter summarized the teaching says in the qurans opening chapter and its three classes of men', '');
', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'al anwaar al lateefah volume 1 the oneness tawheed origination from nothing', 'origination from nothing before anything existed where was the world that was about to be made the answer is stranger than nowhere there was no where at all the teaching turns from the gnosis of the ranks to the act that produced them summarizing a long exposition of sayyidna mohyuddin the originator brought the world of origination into being in a single instant from no prior matter no concurrent matter and no underlying place an act utterly unlike the making we know which only reshapes what already exists he created not from need for a god who needed his creation would be a god in lack but from pure favor drawing the existents out of a nothingness that was no place at all what he brought forth were luminous imaginal forms on which the human body was later patterned the soul a fallen copy of the form the body a fallen copy of the soul so that salvation is a return from dark density toward luminous subtlety and he created all the forms perfectly equal in their first perfection as an act of the justice that gives to none more and to none less', '');
', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'al anwaar al lateefah volume 1 the oneness tawheed equal but not infallible', 'equal but not infallible if every being was created perfectly equal with nothing to separate the first from the last how did anything ever go wrong the teaching answers by drawing out what follows from the absence of any obstacle in the abode of origination the whole order came into being not in time but in a single instant sunlight flooding the air fire filling a dark room with the potential and the actual intellects existing together and no interval between the first perfection and the second the equal forms though created without the slightest disparity were not yet infallible and error the teaching makes precise is exactly the failure to attain the second perfection whether by ones own slipping or by making others slip from that trial state of free equality one form looked at its own essence recognized an originator unlike it and its kind and negated affirmed and bore witness in a single act becoming the first possessor of tawhid and reaching toward the originator through the means of his own unreachable greatness', '');
', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'al anwaar al lateefah volume 1 the oneness tawheed the word and the greatest name', 'the word and the greatest name what single sentence could contain everything that has ever happened and everything that ever will and end by design at the number seven in answer to the first forms seeking of means the divine supports descended and there connected with him the word of allah the testimony of oneness above the intellect and below the originator the link through which all knowledge and light flow for as long as creation endures through that word the first intellect came to encompass all that was and will be but only after first negating himself for self negation always precedes the gift the words numbered composition two three five four seven twelve nineteen is the skeleton showing through scripture the opening formula of the quran the seven imams and their twelve deputies and the originated world itself and knowledge was seen to deepen reverence so that it is the learned who most fear allah the first intellect was raised to be allahs veil gate and greatest name the sole means to the seeking the discourse and the declaring of oneness which is why allegiance to the wali is the only door to tawhid against his success stands the second emanation undone not by denial but by the delusion that his vision equaled the first intellects while above them all stands the circle of oneness that belongs to the originator alone so the first canopy of this book of lights is brought to its close', '');
